  "body": "This is the first slice of #287: a read-only **Machines** pane that browses machine configurations and validates them, naming each refusal. Create, edit and save, and \"Use for this setup\", are follow-ups (#287 stays open).\n\n## What changed\n**App layer** (`crates/app/src/machine/`):\n- `library.rs` builds the machine catalogue: the built-in machines, plus the `.mch` the document mounted through Load other.\n  - Each entry carries its kind, axes, rotaries and units.\n  - It also lists the posts that can drive the machine: the built-in posts for which `posting::post_serves` is true.\n  - A `scan_dir` hook is ready for a user folder.\n- `validate.rs` returns named refusals as `key: rule`, read from the raw JSON (`parse_mch` silently drops a backwards travel). It checks:\n  - travel min < max;\n  - stated feeds and speeds > 0;\n  - codes are well formed;\n  - the keys each machine kind requires are present.\n  - A malformed file is refused by name.\n- `sheet.rs` builds the read-only property sheet, grouped as General, Axes, Spindle, Tool station, Coolants and Posts, in the file's own unit.\n\n**UI:**\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/machines_pane.rs`: a dockable pane opened from the ribbon's View dropdown, with a list, a sheet and the validation result.\n- Opening the pane and selecting a machine are view state, never commands, following the existing panel convention. No project data changes, so nothing goes on the undo history.\n\n`docs/decisions/287-machines-pane.md` records the slice boundary and the user-folder decision, which is posted on #287.\n\n## Readings\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test machine_library`: 11/11 pass.\n- `--test machine`: 32/32 pass.\n- `camcraft-ui --lib machines_pane`: 3/3 pass.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `scripts/gate.sh quick upstream/main`:\n  - app: all pass.\n  - ui: only the known reds that also fail on upstream main:\n    - the GPU headless tests `headless_run_succeeds`, `headless_cli_exit_code_is_zero` and `egui_headless_cli_exit_code_is_zero`;\n    - the `egui_shell_snapshot_light` and `tool_editor_snapshot` goldens (#255).\n- After that gate, the branch merged upstream/main again; the narrow tests still pass.\n- All 10 registered shipped machines validate clean. `3axis-vmc.mch` is the post's static `DEFAULT_MCH` and is not a registered machine, so it is not listed.\n\n## Pinning tests\n- **App:**\n  - `every_shipped_machine_lists_and_validates_clean`\n  - `every_machine_file_in_assets_is_in_the_library`\n  - `backwards_travel_refuses_naming_the_axis`\n  - `non_positive_feeds_and_speeds_refuse_by_name`\n  - `malformed_codes_refuse_by_name`\n  - `required_keys_per_kind_refuse_by_name`\n  - `other_stated_values_refuse_by_name`\n  - `malformed_files_refuse_by_name_and_never_panic`\n  - `a_user_file_lists_by_its_model_and_an_unreadable_one_by_name`\n  - `the_catalogue_adds_the_documents_machine_file`\n  - `a_good_crafted_mill_validates_clean`\n- **UI (structural, no golden PNGs):**\n  - `the_view_door_opens_the_machines_pane_beside_properties`\n  - `selecting_a_shipped_machine_shows_its_sheet_and_a_clean_validation`\n  - `a_refused_machine_file_shows_each_refusal_by_name`\n\n## Not exercised\n- No GUI hand test yet; a test binary has been built for the maintainer.\n- There is no user machines folder yet (decision posted on #287).\n- An AGENTS.md (`assets/machines/AGENTS.md`) changed, so run `/graphify . --update` after merge.\n\nChangelog: Machines pane (View > Machines): browse the built-in and loaded machine files and see each one's properties and validation refusals by name (#287)\n\nRefs #287\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
